            <ArticleTitle>Treatment of left main coronary artery lesion after late thoracic radiotherapy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e53-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0066-782X2011001200018</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Prevention of late cardiovascular complications after radiation therapy (RT) for treatment of a malignant tumor is challenging. We report the case of a young male patient with Hodgkin's lymphoma treated with RT, who developed ischemic heart disease during follow-up, although he had no cardiovascular risk factors. We conclude that patients undergoing RT who experience chest pain should be fully investigated for coronary artery disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
